# PFM Tracking — core rules

- Follow `docs/dev-plan.md` and `AGENTS.md`. Do not invent alternate architectures.
- ShipBob tracking = `GET /2026-07/shipments-tracking` with **repeated** `ShipmentIds=` query params (max 25). Never comma-separate IDs.
- Do not use `/shipment/{id}/timeline` — it 404s.
- No WooCommerce on the runtime order path.
- Polling only in v1; no webhooks.
- `tracking_events` is append-only; status is derived, not blindly overwritten.
- `is_stalled` is a boolean flag, not an internal_status value.
- Never commit `.env` or secrets.
- Public lookup requires order number + email/postcode (never order number alone).
- Customer page reads DB/cache only — never call ShipBob/TrackingMore on page render.
